  <prompt>Implement the H4-shared KV secrets-population handler as an IProvisioningHandler in the L2 control-plane. H4-shared is the SIBLING of H4 (per-tenant) — it seeds SHARED-tier KV secrets by EXTRACTING credentials from source Azure services (AI Search admin key, Cognitive Services key1, Service Bus root SAS, Storage connection string, Redis composed connection string) and writing them to the shared KV under canonical secret names that match the App Service `@Microsoft.KeyVault(SecretName=...)` references. Extends task 084's canonical secret-catalog manifest with a `source: { type, service-ref, key-selector? }` field on shared-tier entries. Idempotent: verify existing secret matches current source; only rotate on drift (audit-logged).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in IProvisioningHandler contract, Azure Key Vault + RBAC (Secrets Officer for write; Secrets User for read), az CLI extraction commands (cognitiveservices keys list, search admin-key show, servicebus namespace authorization-rule keys list, storage account show-connection-string, redis show + list-keys), ADR-028's 21 MUSTs for auth ceremony, and Phase G canonical KV naming (§7.9). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>File src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/SharedKvSourceExtraction/H4SharedKvSourceExtractionHandler.cs exists, implements IProvisioningHandler, registers in L2 DI, and: (a) reads canonical secret-catalog manifest (extended per task 084) filtered to entries with a `source` field; (b) for each entry, extracts value from the named source Azure service via az CLI (per-source-type recipe); (c) writes to shared KV under canonical name (respects existing H4 KV writer + RBAC assumptions); (d) idempotent — if secret exists on KV, compares against fresh source value; NO-OP if match, rotates + audit-logs if drift; (e) never overwrites BINDING never-delete secrets (Dataverse-ClientSecret, BFF-API-ClientSecret) — those come from H4 per-tenant flow, not from source-extraction; (f) sequences BEFORE H4b (task 201) which reads these secrets via KV refs. Unit tests cover: 6-source-type happy path (all F19 sources), source-drift rotation, existing-and-matching NO-OP, source-service-missing quarantine, BINDING guard, idempotency, cleartext-secret leak check.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
Per lessons-learned-model1-prod-standup-2026-08-22.md finding F19 + Automation Gaps roadmap item 12 in `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md`: Bicep provisions the shared KV `sprk-{env}-kv` but leaves it EMPTY. All 6 BFF `@Microsoft.KeyVault(...)` references point to non-existent secrets. Even after F16 fixes (RBAC + kvRefIdentity), refs cannot resolve. BFF fails-fast at boot on the downstream config chain (F20/F20a).

This session (2026-08-24) manually seeded 6 secrets to `sprk-prod-kv` by extracting from source services via ad-hoc bash. Recipe worked; this task codifies the recipe as an IProvisioningHandler.

The extraction recipes (validated live this session):
- `AiSearch--AdminKey`  ← `az search admin-key show --service-name sprksharedprod-search --resource-group rg-spaarke-shared-prod --query primaryKey -o tsv`
- `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey`  ← `az cognitiveservices account keys list --name sprksharedprod-docintel --resource-group rg-spaarke-shared-prod --query key1 -o tsv`
- `AzureOpenAI-ApiKey`  ← `az cognitiveservices account keys list --name sprksharedprod-openai --resource-group rg-spaarke-shared-prod --query key1 -o tsv`
- `servicebus-connection-string`  ← `az servicebus namespace authorization-rule keys list --namespace-name sprksharedprod-servicebus --resource-group rg-spaarke-shared-prod --name RootManageSharedAccessKey --query primaryConnectionString -o tsv`
- `storage-connection-string`  ← `az storage account show-connection-string --name sprksharedprodsa --resource-group rg-spaarke-shared-prod --query connectionString -o tsv`
- `redis-connection-string`  ← composed as `{host}:{port},password={primaryKey},ssl=True,abortConnect=False` from `az redis show` + `az redis list-keys`

CLUSTER FINDING (from SESSION 2 handoff): F17 + F19 + F20 share ONE root cause — Bicep provisions Model 1 Prod infra but does NOT seed BFF runtime state. H4-shared + H4b (task 201) + H9 (BFF deploy) together close this gap. Sequencing: H4-shared → H4b → H9 → BFF starts with all config in place (kills F20 progressive fail-fast).
    </background>
