  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Single IProvisioningHandler implementation registered in L2 DI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register in L2 control-plane, NOT BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Auth ceremony 21 MUSTs; source-extraction runs as the L2 UAMI (which must hold data-plane read on each source: `Cognitive Services User`, `Search Service Contributor` for admin-key, `Azure Service Bus Data Owner` for SAS, `Storage Account Contributor` for connection-string, `Redis Cache Contributor` for list-keys).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Reuse background-job infrastructure; return 202; fire-and-forget.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency key: kv-shared-{env}-{secretsVer} — secretsVer is manifest hash from Phase H canonical secret-catalog (source-scoped entries).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Extends task 084 manifest schema: shared-tier entries carry `source: { type: 'ai-search-admin-key' | 'cognitive-services-key1' | 'service-bus-root-sas' | 'storage-connection-string' | 'redis-composed', service-ref: '<az-resource-name>' }`. Generator (Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1) fans out extraction wiring per entry.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Per-source-type extraction recipes are declarative (map source-type → az CLI command template with service-ref substitution). NO ad-hoc bash. NO shelling out to per-secret one-off scripts.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency: for each entry, compare current KV value against fresh source extraction; NO-OP if match, rotate + audit-log if drift. Drift may indicate source-key rotation in Azure Portal (legitimate) OR unauthorized change (audit signal).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BINDING guard: NEVER overwrite Dataverse-ClientSecret or BFF-API-ClientSecret via this handler. Those secrets have no `source` field in the manifest — they come from H4 per-tenant flow. Handler asserts these secret names never appear in H4-shared's target set.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §7.9">Canonical KV secret naming applied at seed time: env-agnostic names; secret names MUST match the App Service `@Microsoft.KeyVault(SecretName=...)` references exactly (case-sensitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md NFR-05">BFF /health must fail fast at boot on any Tier-1 IOptions misconfig — H4-shared runs BEFORE H4b + BEFORE H9 so that when BFF eventually boots, all KV refs resolve.</constraint>
    <constraint source="F15+F18-remediation">Handler MUST assume L2 UAMI has already been granted `Key Vault Secrets Officer` on the shared KV via H4-preflight (task-TODO for operator-RBAC bootstrap; F15/F18 both fixed manually this session — pre-check runs BEFORE H4-shared writes).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-§10">L2 handlers register in L2 DI, NOT in BFF (§10 BFF Hygiene). Publish-size verification applies to BFF only; L2 has its own separate deploy footprint.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-§11">NEW-surface justification field completed per §11 three-question gate (see &lt;justification&gt; below).</constraint>
  </constraints>

