  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load knowledge files. Verify task 084 manifest schema is extensible (v2 schema field addition is additive — no v1-consumer break).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Extend manifest schema">Add `source: { type, service-ref, key-selector? }` field to shared-tier entries in scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml. Add the initial 6-entry F19 manifest (AiSearch--AdminKey, DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey, AzureOpenAI-ApiKey, servicebus-connection-string, storage-connection-string, redis-connection-string).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Extend generator">Update Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 to emit source-extraction wiring per entry (e.g., generates a C# `SharedKvSecretSource` record set consumed by the handler). Deterministic output preserved.</step>
    <step order="3" name="ISourceExtractor abstraction">Author ISourceExtractor.cs with `Task&lt;string&gt; ExtractAsync(SharedKvSecretSource source, CancellationToken ct)`. AzCliSourceExtractor implements per-source-type recipes (ai-search-admin-key / cognitive-services-key1 / service-bus-root-sas / storage-connection-string / redis-composed). Each recipe shells to az CLI with declarative arg composition (no string concat of user input).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Handler impl">Author H4SharedKvSourceExtractionHandler.cs — inject ISourceExtractor, IKvSecretsWriter (reused from H4), IArmKeyVaultRefProbe, IIdempotencyService, ICosmosRunStore. HandleAsync: (a) load manifest entries with `source` field; (b) BINDING guard: assert no entry name matches never-delete list; (c) for each entry: extract fresh source value → compare against current KV value → NO-OP on match, WriteAsync + audit on drift or absence; (d) idempotency key `kv-shared-{env}-{secretsVer}`.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Post-condition verification">After all writes, invoke IArmKeyVaultRefProbe to verify each canonical name is now resolvable via the App Service KV-ref binding (uses F16-remediated kvRefIdentity path). If any ref fails to resolve, quarantine with clear diagnostic pointing to F16 / operator-RBAC gaps.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Redis composed recipe">Implement the `redis-composed` extractor as documented in F19: (a) `az redis show --name X --resource-group Y --query "{host:hostName,port:sslPort}" -o json`; (b) `az redis list-keys --name X --resource-group Y --query primaryKey -o tsv`; (c) compose `{host}:{port},password={key},ssl=True,abortConnect=False`. Escape values for shell (extractor never string-concats user data; uses az CLI's -o tsv for terminated output).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Cleartext-secret leak scan">Verify extracted values NEVER appear in log statements, Cosmos parameters, or interStepState. All logs must redact (log first 4 chars + `***`).</step>
    <step order="8" name="Unit tests">Author unit tests: (a) 6-source-type happy path with mocked ISourceExtractor returning known values; (b) source-drift rotation (KV has "old", source returns "new" → WriteAsync + audit-log); (c) existing-and-matching NO-OP (KV == source → no write, no audit); (d) source-service-missing quarantine (extractor throws HttpRequestException / az CLI exit non-zero → QuarantineRequired); (e) BINDING guard (manifest tampered to include Dataverse-ClientSecret in source-entries → handler fails startup validation); (f) idempotency (two runs same secretsVer → second is no-op); (g) cleartext-leak scan (grep unit test: assert Cosmos + logs contain no secret substrings); (h) manifest-schema-v1 backwards compat (entries without `source` field are skipped, not errored).</step>
    <step order="9" name="Program.cs registration">Register H4SharedKvSourceExtractionHandler + ISourceExtractor → AzCliSourceExtractor in L2 Program.cs DI. Wire into HandlerIds catalog (task 103 owns the keyed-DI pattern).</step>
    <step order="10" name="Build + test">Run `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/` + `dotnet test`. Verify green + zero analyzer warnings.</step>
    <step order="11" name="Handler-catalog update">Update handler catalog in `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md` Step 3 handler enumeration to list H4-shared alongside H4 (main-session-only per root CLAUDE.md §3 sub-agent write boundary).</step>
    <step order="12" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 200 → ✅ (main-session-only if TASK-INDEX.md is inside `.claude/` — verify path).</step>
    <step order="13" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If task 084 manifest schema does NOT yet exist OR does not accept additive `source` field without breaking v1 consumers, STOP and escalate: task 084 must land first, or H4-shared must be blocked at &lt;gate&gt;.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any source Azure service is unreachable during H4-shared (extractor gets 403 despite Bicep having provisioned + F15/F18-style RBAC granted), STOP and quarantine — root cause is L2 UAMI missing `Cognitive Services User` / `Search Service Contributor` / `Azure Service Bus Data Owner` / `Storage Account Contributor` / `Redis Cache Contributor` (5 new RBAC assignments Bicep must emit for L2 UAMI on every source service). Do NOT retry-loop; escalate for Bicep hardening.</trigger>
    <trigger>If IArmKeyVaultRefProbe verify-step fails after H4-shared writes (secret is on KV but App Service can't resolve the ref), STOP and escalate — F16 remediation gap OR kvRefIdentity misconfig. Do NOT proceed to H4b.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a manifest entry lists a source-type not yet implemented in AzCliSourceExtractor, STOP and escalate — the manifest MUST NOT get ahead of the extractor. New source-types are a small design decision (add a recipe + a test); do NOT invent extractor logic on the fly.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbors: (a) H4 per-tenant handler (task 047) — writes to per-tenant KV using literal values from `IKvSecretManifest`; NO source-extraction. (b) Manual ad-hoc bash extracted 6 F19 secrets this session — no automation. (c) `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` (task 084) — has canonical names + never-delete flags, but NO source-extraction schema. Grep for `SourceExtractor` returns none across codebase.</existing>
    <extension>No — H4 per-tenant CANNOT be extended to also do source-extraction because (a) different KV scope (shared vs per-tenant), (b) different manifest entries (literal vs source-linked), (c) different idempotency semantics (H4 rotation-safe by default; H4-shared verifies against fresh source every run and rotates on drift). Wrapping them into ONE handler would require conditional branches on every step. Two sibling handlers keep each contract tight.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without H4-shared as a handler: (1) Every new Model 1 shared-tier deploy needs manual ad-hoc bash to seed 6 secrets (this session burned ~30 min doing so; multiplied across N future customer stand-ups = N × 30 min waste). (2) Every source-service key rotation (Azure Portal → regenerate key1) silently breaks BFF startup until an operator manually re-seeds the KV — no drift detection today. (3) Model 2 Dedicated tier (per-customer, future) will hit the SAME F19 pattern with per-customer source services; without H4-shared's source-extraction primitive, we would re-invent it for M2. The failure mode is concrete: BFF fails-fast at boot on `Unhandled exception. System.InvalidOperationException` for any of the 6 KV-referenced app settings — observed live this session as F20 chain.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

