  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a manifest with 6 source-extraction entries (F19 canonical set), when HandleAsync runs against a shared KV with no prior secrets, then all 6 secrets are written to KV under canonical names via IKvSecretsWriter; each write is preceded by an ISourceExtractor call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency-NO-OP: given the same manifest + KV state, second HandleAsync invocation performs 6 source-extractions (to verify current values) + 0 KV writes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency-DRIFT-ROTATE: given a mocked source-drift for one entry, HandleAsync performs 1 rotation write for that entry + 0 writes for the other 5; audit log records the rotation with entry name + old-value-hash + new-value-hash (never the values themselves).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BINDING guard: given a tampered manifest that lists Dataverse-ClientSecret as a source-extraction entry, HandleAsync fails startup validation with "BindingPreCheckViolation" BEFORE any extractor or writer is called.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-condition ref-resolution: after all writes, IArmKeyVaultRefProbe verifies each canonical secret name resolves via the App Service KV-ref binding; failure → Quarantine with diagnostic pointing to F16 / operator-RBAC gaps.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Source-unreachable Quarantine: given a mocked ISourceExtractor that throws (simulating az CLI exit non-zero), HandleAsync quarantines the run with clear diagnostic naming the failed service.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency-key match: two invocations for the same (env, secretsVer) — second call short-circuits before source extraction (kv-shared-{env}-{secretsVer} match).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cleartext-secret leak scan: unit test greps Cosmos parameters + interStepState + all log statements for known secret patterns (test-manifest secret values); assert 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Manifest-schema-v1 backwards compat: entries in the manifest WITHOUT a `source` field are skipped by H4-shared (they belong to H4 per-tenant flow); no error, no warning.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler registers in L2 DI; `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/` + `dotnet test` exit 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler catalog in `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md` Step 3 enumeration includes H4-shared alongside H4 (main-session write).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Sequencing verified: H4-shared runs BEFORE H4b (task 201) AND BEFORE H9 (BFF deploy) in the L2 state machine's handler DAG.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: lessons-learned-model1-prod-standup-2026-08-22.md finding F19 + Automation Gaps roadmap item 12 + spec.md FR-36 canonical-manifest + design.md §4.1 H4 (sibling). Companion task: 201 (H4b-BulkAppSettings). This session (2026-08-24) manually validated all 6 source-extraction recipes against Model 1 Prod — the recipes ARE the design contract. Live-fire test bed: Model 1 Prod (`sprksharedprod-*` source services + `sprk-prod-kv` shared vault).

## Design notes (2026-08-24, SESSION 3 — H4b/H4-shared design)

**Rationale for splitting from H4 (task 047)**:
- H4 is a per-tenant handler with rotation-SAFE default (never overwrites unless H4-rotate variant).
- H4-shared is a shared-tier handler with drift-DETECTION default (verifies against source every run; rotates on drift).
- Different idempotency semantics → different handler.
- Different KV scope (per-tenant vs shared) → different write target.
- Different manifest entries (literal-value vs source-linked) → different reader path.

**Bicep hardening implications (NEW work implied by this task)**:
- L2 UAMI needs 5 new RBAC assignments on source services: `Cognitive Services User` (on `sprksharedprod-openai` + `sprksharedprod-docintel`), `Search Service Contributor` (on `sprksharedprod-search`), `Azure Service Bus Data Owner` (on `sprksharedprod-servicebus`), `Storage Account Contributor` (on `sprksharedprodsa`), `Redis Cache Contributor` (on `sprksharedprod-redis`). Emit as Bicep in `stacks/model1-shared.bicep` (or `platform-shared.bicep` if it exists). File as a follow-on task if not already covered by Wave C UAMI migration (task 030).

**Model 2 Dedicated extensibility**: the manifest schema field `source: { type, service-ref }` naturally extends to per-customer source services (Model 2 Dedicated has 1:1 env-per-customer, so service-refs become customer-scoped). H4-shared → H4-tenant-source variant is a natural M2 follow-on with the same handler shape.
  </notes>

